Package: libva-av1fix
Version: 2.23.0+av1fix3
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: TheMojoMan <themojoman@gmx.net>
Depends: libc6
Description: libva 2.23.0 with the AV1 refresh-frame flag pass-through (erhai)
 Upstream libva 2.23.0 plus av1fix-patches/0001: VADecPictureParameterBufferAV1
 learned refresh_frame_flags and refresh_frame_flags_valid, and libva passes
 them through to the driver.
 .
 iris-vaapi cannot recover the AV1 refresh set from ref_frame_map[] alone (the
 map describes the DPB BEFORE the picture is stored), so without these fields
 the driver has to guess, and on real 1080p/4K streams that guess loses
 references.  ffmpeg carries the same information with av1fix-patches/0002.
 .
 Built with libva's driver directory at the distro path
 /usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/dri, so the iris driver is found where
 oneplus-erhai-video installs it and no second copy is needed.
 .
 Installed as a /usr/local drop-in (it wins over Ubuntu's libva.so.2 in the
 loader path), so the distro package is neither replaced nor diverted, and
 libva-x11/libva-drm stay Ubuntu's own.  Built without X11/GLX/Wayland
 backends — the display helpers live in those separate distro libraries.
